// PURPOSE: Load six safe, synthetic messages for the demonstration.
//
// Run this after files 01 through 06. Eventhouse downloads the public sample
// file, applies RawTelemetryJsonMapping, and adds the messages to RawTelemetry.
// The update policies then run automatically and populate the clean tables and
// drift observations. The sample includes normal data, new fields, an
// incompatible value, multiple zones, and an empty zone list.
//
// multijson means the source contains one complete JSON object per line.
// Important: use raw.githubusercontent.com. A github.com/.../blob/... link is
// an HTML page for browsers, not the JSONL file, and ingestion will fail with
// ExtentId 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000 and HasErrors=true.
.ingest into table RawTelemetry
('https://raw.githubusercontent.com/MatthieuLefebvre/eventhouse-schema-drift-reference/main/samples/telemetry.jsonl')
with (
    format='multijson',
    ingestionMappingReference='RawTelemetryJsonMapping'
)

// Run this after the ingestion operation completes. The expected result is 6.
RawTelemetry
| summarize IngestedRows=count()

// If HasErrors is true, replace the example ID below with the OperationId from
// the .ingest response to retrieve the service's detailed error message.
// .show ingestion failures
// | where tostring(OperationId) == '00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000'
// | project FailedOn, Details, RootActivityId, OperationId
